Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.21,0:00:23.84,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,There you are, you bastards!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.84,0:00:27.84,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,Give back the 50,000,000 gold \Nyou took from me!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.92,0:00:34.29,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I see. You sold your weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.29,0:00:35.59,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Run for it, Ruche!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.59,0:00:36.31,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.30,0:00:39.84,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,You're not getting away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.06,0:00:45.20,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Hilde.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.74,0:00:58.10,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Is that the Heavy Knight?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:13.00,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,This aura, this intensity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.93,0:01:22.94,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,This must be the real \NBlackened Flameblade.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.44,0:01:30.95,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,This is them, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.37,0:01:35.90,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,They used underhanded \Nmethods to steal my money!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.48,0:01:43.66,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.49,0:01:47.10,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,My class is Magic Swordsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.06,0:01:50.63,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I'm an A-rank adventurer.\NMy name is Carlos.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.61,0:01:55.64,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I wanted to meet you \Nafter Hilde told me about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.69,0:02:02.69,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Elymas the Heavy Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.08,0:03:51.42,sign_generic,EPTITLE; sign,0,0,0,,{\b1\fnTimes New Roman\an7\bord1\shad1.25\fade(1420,482)\alphaalphaH&0&\3c&H000000&\c&HFEFCFD&\4c&H000000&\fs15\pos(398.78,291.342)}Episode 21\h\h\h\h\h\hBlackened Flameblade
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.01,0:03:58.63,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Forgive me, but there's something \NI must confirm first.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.03,0:04:03.14,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Is it true that you cheated Hilde \Nout of her money?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.52,0:04:11.02,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,The Blackened Flameblade \Nis truly powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.52,0:04:15.53,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,If we fought him now, \Nwe wouldn't stand a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.53,0:04:18.54,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,She demanded we\Ngive her our Mythril Sword,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.90,0:04:21.91,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,so we settled the matter with a duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.33,0:04:23.69,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,This was the result.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.76,0:04:34.92,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I thought so.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.93,0:04:42.22,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.22,0:04:45.22,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,M-Master, what was that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.64,0:04:49.89,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I figured that was the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.89,0:04:54.15,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,What? But you said you believed me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.15,0:04:57.36,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I only said to take me to them \Nbecause I wanted to meet them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.41,0:05:04.87,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Hilde, you keep calling me Master, \Nbut I don't consider myself your master.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.87,0:05:07.96,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,What? M-Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.77,0:05:17.38,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I suppose saying that now sounds like \NI'm trying to evade responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.50,0:05:23.23,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,It seems you were rather inconvenienced \Nas a result of my negligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.23,0:05:25.89,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,N-Not at all. I don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.31,0:05:29.89,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I merely accepted her challenge \Nto make a bit of money.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.89,0:05:31.81,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I could've declined.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.30,0:05:37.19,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,When I was still new, \NI didn't have the greatest allies.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.19,0:05:41.20,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,As a result, I believe I'm \Na good judge of character.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.72,0:05:45.45,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,You're a good man, Elymas.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.45,0:05:49.17,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,He's such a good guy, I'm starting \Nto feel uncomfortable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.17,0:05:52.21,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,I don't understand how his \Nstudent turned out like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.83,0:05:56.96,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,As for the money…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.96,0:06:01.09,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,For her sake, don't give it back to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.96,0:06:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&HF6B0F7&\3cFFFFFF\pos(330,185)}ack
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.72,0:06:05.22,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,She only learns from \Nnegative consequences.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.22,0:06:07.22,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Uh, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.22,0:06:10.93,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I have another request for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.16,0:06:15.31,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,But let's speak elsewhere. \NJoin me for lunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.31,0:06:29.24,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,So, what's your request?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.24,0:06:36.00,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Recently, odd monster disasters \Nare on the rise around Lacoryna.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.92,0:06:40.30,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,It's a genuinely strange development.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.30,0:06:43.97,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Monsters come pouring out of \Nbrand new dungeons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.69,0:06:48.10,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Extremely rare Existence Evolutions \Nare occurring one after another.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.67,0:06:55.09,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Is this just a coincidence \Nor is there a reason for this trend?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.09,0:06:59.02,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I've been conducting my own investigation \Nby visiting Lacoryna's dungeons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.53,0:07:04.27,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,The Adventurer's Guild acquired \Nnew information recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.27,0:07:08.48,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,It seems certain that something's afoot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.17,0:07:12.28,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Are you referring \Nto the Centipede's Gallery?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.28,0:07:16.58,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,You're a skilled adventurer \Nif you already know about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.04,0:07:21.50,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,For nearly two weeks, \NI've been investigating on my own,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.40,0:07:25.41,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,but I failed to conquer a certain dungeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.41,0:07:28.51,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,You failed? But you're rank A.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.55,0:07:36.52,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Dungeons too difficult for a rank A \Nshouldn't spawn around Lacoryna.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.84,0:07:39.20,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,A Monster Pool appeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.91,0:07:43.19,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,There was nothing I could do by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.53,0:07:49.62,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,A Monster Pool is when an abnormal number \Nof monsters pour out of a dungeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.39,0:07:54.15,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,It was one of the monster disasters \Nfeared in{\i0} Magic World{\i1} as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.91,0:07:58.71,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,As I thought, that Death Amude \Nwasn't the only incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.79,0:08:04.21,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Something must be\Ntriggering these disasters.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.57,0:08:09.97,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,If the frequency of monster-related\Ndisasters increases everywhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.02,0:08:15.65,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,the habitable area for humans \Nwill shrink significantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.65,0:08:16.23,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.23,0:08:19.79,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I-It can't be that bad, Mr. Elymas.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.79,0:08:22.15,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,You must be exaggerating.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.66,0:08:26.15,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,At the very least, I don't think he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.10,0:08:28.68,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I agree with Elymas.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.72,0:08:36.05,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,So let's get down to business.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.51,0:08:40.83,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I'd like to invite you on a raid quest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.40,0:08:46.09,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,The dungeon I retreated from \Nis the Graveyard of Grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.09,0:08:49.29,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I'd like your help investigating \Nand conquering it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.09,0:08:56.43,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,If this were an ordinary Monster Pool, \NI'd be in no rush to defeat it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.43,0:08:58.52,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,But that dungeon is new.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.52,0:09:02.88,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,The conditions for a monster disaster \Nshouldn't have been met yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.72,0:09:07.86,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,The situation could get worse \Nif it isn't addressed soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.46,0:09:15.37,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,What should we do, Mr. Elymas?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.98,0:09:22.19,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Normally, I'd say yes immediately, \Nbut I have a few concerns.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.19,0:09:23.13,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.44,0:09:27.90,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,We'll have an A-rank adventurer with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.90,0:09:31.88,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,He's a Magic Swordsman \Nwho taught Hilde when to retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.18,0:09:33.88,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,They won't do anything reckless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.88,0:09:37.14,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Even so, there's something \Nominous about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.35,0:09:39.28,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Still…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.05,0:09:45.02,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I want to go regardless.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.24,0:09:57.58,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,If something strange really is happening \Nin this world, it can only be stopped
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.94,0:10:03.10,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,by me and my extensive\Nmemories of playing {\i0}Magic World{\i1}.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.14,0:10:09.13,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,It's been a while since we last \Nfought side by side.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.70,0:10:12.15,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Hilde, you don't have to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.15,0:10:14.76,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,What?! Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.37,0:10:16.96,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I'm kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.57,0:10:47.64,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Under Carlos's command, Ruche \Nand I embarked on a raid quest
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.64,0:10:50.89,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,to investigate and conquer \Nthe Graveyard of Grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.37,0:11:07.02,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Big city guilds can mobilize a lot more \Nhigh-level adventurers than others.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.34,0:11:11.97,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,They must really trust Mr. Carlos, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.97,0:11:13.28,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,That's true.
