Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.15,0:11:23.78,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Since Veruga completed my Mythril\NSword and Blacksteel Armor in time,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.78,0:11:25.26,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,I'm well-equipped.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.79,0:11:30.08,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Now, people will stop treating me \Nlike a novice Heavy Knight in Iron Armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.08,0:11:31.33,Default,MARY,0,0,0,,Elymas!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.21,0:11:34.57,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,The Sea Dragon's Fang \Ndecided to come along?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.04,0:11:39.01,Default,MARY,0,0,0,,We can't fish if the dungeons \Nare screwed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.32,0:11:42.26,Default,MARY,0,0,0,,Let's see what you can do besides fish.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.26,0:11:44.69,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I'm excited to see your other skills, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.72,0:11:46.92,Default,MARY,0,0,0,,For fishing!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.92,0:11:48.35,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,For fishing!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.11,0:11:51.40,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,A-Aren't we doing this to save the world?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.40,0:11:52.86,Default,EYEPATCH,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.40,0:12:03.12,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,Master, did we really need \Nthis many people?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.46,0:12:07.87,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,I'm not so sure. \NA few healers would be enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.08,0:12:14.55,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,The situation could've gotten worse, \Nso I recruited a few extra people.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.82,0:12:19.05,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,There's no point in bringing \Na bunch of dead weight.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.49,0:12:23.01,Default,ADVENTURER 5,0,0,0,,Why's the Blackened Flameblade's \Nstudent wielding a scythe?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.49,0:12:28.02,Default,ADVENTURER 4,0,0,0,,Who knows? Maybe she picked up \Na scythe Skill Tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.02,0:12:31.27,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,She tried to borrow \Na spare weapon from Carlos,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.05,0:12:35.28,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,but he told her to sit with \Nthe consequences of her actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.61,0:12:33.62,flashbacktop,CARLOS,0,0,0,,No. Keep using that scythe.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.73,0:12:35.28,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fade(189,1)\t(189,1480,\fs30)\b1\move(209.778,81.556,208,68.444,189,1480)\c&H90F1F1&}Shock
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.62,0:12:35.28,flashbacktop,HILDE,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.78,0:12:40.95,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I wonder why Mr. Carlos took \NMs. Hilde on as a student.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.95,0:12:43.47,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,Sorry you don't approve!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.24,0:12:47.50,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry! That's not what I meant!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.72,0:12:53.38,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I haven't done anything \Nto earn the title of master.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.73,0:12:57.05,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I believe Magic Swordsman \Nis a strong class.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.34,0:13:02.22,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Its offensive capabilities are strong, \Nbut it's resource hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.51,0:13:05.65,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,That often puts us at odds \Nwith our party members.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.65,0:13:08.98,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Without guidance, she'd end up \Nisolated in the guild and go astray.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.46,0:13:13.60,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I could see that she'd ultimately die \Ndoing something reckless by herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.52,0:13:21.53,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,In {\i0}Magic World{\i1}, what benefited a Magic\NSwordsman often didn't benefit the party.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.53,0:13:23.27,Default,MAGIC SWORDSMAN,0,0,0,,You guys handle the trash mobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.27,0:13:24.78,Default,MAGIC SWORDSMAN,0,0,0,,I'll focus on the boss.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.78,0:13:25.58,Default,PARTY MEMBER A,0,0,0,,That's not fair!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.58,0:13:26.95,Default,PARTY MEMBER B,0,0,0,,Don't be selfish!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.68,0:13:31.12,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Impatience prevents us from \Nseeing the world as others do.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.43,0:13:34.50,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I was like that once.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.33,0:13:39.60,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I was frustrated by their \Nlack of understanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.60,0:13:45.19,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I was impatient to succeed and wondered\Nhow others could be so egotistical.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.05,0:13:53.17,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,I still wish I'd had someone \Nto calmly offer me advice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.77,0:13:59.28,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,That's why I reached out to Hilde.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.81,0:14:07.95,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,My master is an open-minded, \Nstrong, and kind man.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.33,0:14:10.45,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,Pretty impressive, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.81,0:14:14.86,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,If only his student had taken on \Nmore of his personality.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.86,0:14:16.46,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,What was that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.38,0:14:19.59,Default,HILDE,0,0,0,,Don't laugh, insolent girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.61,0:14:32.48,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I can't imagine Mr. Carlos \Never being so troubled.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.78,0:14:37.48,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I think he's exaggerating \Nso Hilde can save face.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.48,0:14:38.86,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.04,0:14:41.23,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Stop, everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.45,0:15:09.18,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,Something's coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.31,0:15:12.68,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\b1\blur1.5\bord1\c&HFFFFDE&\3c&HE1E294&\t(730,1105,\c&HFEFBD5&\3c&HDFAF26&)\an7\fade(250,1)\fs15\pos(400.134,205.556)}Monster: Mad Wolf
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.46,0:15:13.96,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Level 52 right off the bat?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.96,0:15:16.19,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,It's a horde of monsters that \Npoured out of the dungeon!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.01,0:15:18.52,Default,CARLOS,0,0,0,,We'll intercept them!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.93,0:15:23.97,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,If Rondalm were overrun by monsters of \Nthis level, the lord would have to act.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.08,0:15:40.79,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Ruche!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.42,0:15:43.80,italics,SYSTEM VOICE,0,0,0,,Status effect: poisoned.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.88,0:15:45.42,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\b1\fs25\bord1\c&H68BEFA&\3c&H9F2EBD&\fade(396,0)\pos(147.333,208)}Status Effect\N{\b1\alphaFF\t(521,1022,\alpha00)\c&HF830F6&\3c&H500033&} Poisoned
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.80,0:15:45.80,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I poisoned it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.80,0:15:47.54,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Good! That didn't take long!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.93,0:15:51.93,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,It's the effect of Ruche's new weapon, \NPoisonous Chilopoda Dagger.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.58,0:15:58.21,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,With her high Luck and number of attacks, \Nshe's likely to poison her target.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.94,0:16:05.44,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Furthermore, in {\i0}Magic World{\i1}, the poisoned \Nstatus decreases Speed by 10%.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.90,0:16:05.44,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\b1\fs25\bord1\c&H68BEFA&\3c&H9F2EBD&\fade(396,0)\pos(500.222,205.333)}Status Effect\N{\b1\alphaFF\t(521,1022,\alpha00)\c&HF830F6&\3c&H500033&} Poisoned
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.00,0:16:07.90,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Time to end this!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.90,0:16:10.91,italics,SYSTEM VOICE,0,0,0,,Acquired 174 EXP.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.99,0:16:10.91,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fad(606,2)\b1\bord1\shad2\blur0.5\c&H2ADDF5&\3c&H292830&\4c&H292830&\pos(183.026,58.586)}Acquired 174 EXP
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.83,0:16:20.83,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,There are still more enemies!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.18,0:16:22.91,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Keep reducing their numbers!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.58,0:16:24.84,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,O-Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.32,0:16:42.36,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,That's all of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.82,0:16:46.36,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,That was a fierce reception, and we're \Nnot even inside the dungeon yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.16,0:16:50.75,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Looks like your Poisonous Chilopoda \NDagger was effective, Ruche.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.75,0:16:53.87,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Well, my class lacks firepower,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.87,0:16:57.87,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,so I'm glad to have a knife \Nthat inflicts a status effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.29,0:17:00.87,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I feel like I'm suddenly way stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.20,0:17:04.29,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,You took a little damage, \Nthough. Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.57,0:17:08.01,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I got a little too excited \Nabout my new weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.44,0:17:13.68,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I'm totally fine, but do you think I\Nshould use a Healing Potion anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.12,0:17:15.15,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,Heal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.68,0:17:20.69,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you, uh…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.69,0:17:24.16,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,I'm Maebel, a Priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.16,0:17:29.31,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,I was brought along because I'm \Na healing class, but I'm only rank C.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.31,0:17:32.86,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you two rank Bs.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.20,0:17:35.49,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,We're counting on you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.49,0:17:39.13,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,That said, we're actually newbies.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.13,0:17:41.21,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,N-Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.60,0:17:43.48,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,I'm Elymas, a Heavy Knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.48,0:17:45.74,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,This is Ruche, a Pierrot.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.23,0:17:47.46,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,I'm Ruche.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.80,0:17:52.76,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,I'm glad our white magic user \Nseems dependable.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.35,0:17:57.89,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,We're not in the dungeon yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.89,0:18:01.27,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Don't make our healer \Nwaste her precious MP.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.70,0:18:06.93,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,This guy is Kelt, a B-rank hunter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.49,0:18:11.53,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,He's one of the higher-level \Nmembers of this raid quest.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.53,0:18:15.37,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Ignore anyone who goes \Ntoo hard this early.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.72,0:18:20.62,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,I can't believe our healer doesn't \Nknow how to pace themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.62,0:18:26.13,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,Sorry, Mr. Kelt. I'll think \Nharder before I act.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.49,0:18:27.79,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,That's easy to say in hindsight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.79,0:18:29.35,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Against that many enemies,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.35,0:18:33.48,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,it's not a bad idea to prioritize \Nreducing their numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.48,0:18:38.39,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,At the very least, it's not worth making \Nthings awkward by mentioning it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.92,0:18:41.16,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,You don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.16,0:18:43.89,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,This raid quest is a marathon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.20,0:18:46.83,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Our primary goal is investigating \Nthe dungeon interior.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.83,0:18:48.90,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,It's different from a simple search.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.26,0:18:52.85,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Don't stubbornly try to pick \Nfights with me, newbie.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.45,0:19:03.91,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,You're deliberately being \Ndisruptive to assert control.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.33,0:19:12.09,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,His words gave the impression that \Nhe can tell our healer what to do
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.43,0:19:14.93,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,while also curbing our front liners.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.91,0:19:18.39,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,As a Hunter who can pick off \Nmonsters from the back,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.39,0:19:22.22,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Kelt benefits from our \Nfront line being thwarted.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.65,0:19:28.55,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Don't embarrass yourself by \Nrunning your mouth, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.94,0:19:30.94,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Use your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.67,0:19:37.11,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Looks like we got some \Ngood drops this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.82,0:19:42.35,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,Standard practice says they go\Nto whoever landed the killing blow.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.35,0:19:44.25,Default,KELT,0,0,0,,I'll be taking these.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.25,0:19:47.11,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,But those dropped because of my skill.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.07,0:19:53.14,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Don't let him bother you, Maebel.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.14,0:19:56.82,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,His goal from the start was to \Nintimidate us by pointing out our flaws.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.24,0:19:58.63,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.05,0:20:04.31,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,As a healer, guys like him \Nare always messing with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.65,0:20:11.31,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,Besides, if you nod along while \Nmaking up reasons to delay healing them,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.13,0:20:15.32,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,guys like him tend to fall in line.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.32,0:20:18.32,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,There isn't as much space \Ninside the dungeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.32,0:20:24.24,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,Even a Hunter will take damage, \Nand that class's Defense is low.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.24,0:20:29.17,Default,MAEBEL,0,0,0,,I'd like for us to be friends, \Nso I'm counting on you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.17,0:20:30.75,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.08,0:20:33.78,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,We appreciate that.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.24,0:20:41.64,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Maybe long-lived adventurers\N in this world are tougher than I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.85,0:20:49.47,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Looking back, she probably cast that spell \Nto create a positive relationship with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.13,0:20:53.54,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,She didn't need to cast Heal yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.91,0:21:05.81,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,While avoiding and sometimes \Nfighting the undead roaming the area…
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.69,0:21:15.12,italicstop,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,we eventually arrived \Nat the entrance to the Graveyard of Grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.96,0:21:15.84,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\bord0\an7\fade(2350,1)\b1\fs15\pos(210.486,292.99)}Graveyard of Grief Entrance
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.58,0:21:15.84,sign_generic,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fs8\b1\an7\fade(430,1)\pos(535.5,310.202)}Recommended Level: 70
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.25,0:21:18.03,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,This place is aptly named.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.03,0:21:22.09,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,Couldn't they have \Ngiven them proper burials?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.38,0:21:25.16,Default,RUCHE,0,0,0,,They made this dungeon spawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.16,0:21:28.10,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,Maybe there used to be a village nearby.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.62,0:21:32.98,Default,ELYMAS,0,0,0,,The villagers must've either \Ndied out or moved to Lacoryna.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.31,0:21:36.93,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,Something strange is happening here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.93,0:21:38.72,italics,ELYMAS/ID,0,0,0,,I have to figure out what's going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.46,0:23:17.15,italics,ELYMAS/NA,0,0,0,,Ruche and I joined a raid quest group \Nof high-level adventurers.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.68,0:23:20.28,italics,ELYMAS/NA,0,0,0,,We teamed up with new allies,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.28,0:23:23.88,italics,ELYMAS/NA,0,0,0,,and we split into groups to slay \Nas many monsters as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.05,0:23:30.22,italics,ELYMAS/NA,0,0,0,,Kelt and Maebel are both pretty eccentric.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.26,0:23:34.77,italics,ELYMAS/NA,0,0,0,,Next time, "Hunter Kelt \Nand Priest Maebel."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.77,0:23:37.84,italics,ELYMAS/NA,0,0,0,,I hope this is all we have to worry about.

